1. Purpose

Grey M1 solver a la Radice et al. 2022 [arXiv:2111.14858].

This code needs 2 ghost cells on unigrid and 4 ghost cells with AMR.

A. Acknowledgements

This code is ported from THC_M1 (https://bitbucket.org/FreeTHC/thccore/src/master/) of Radice et al. 

B. NuRates population-dependent collisions

For rates_lib="NuRates", a local six-variable spectral solve updates all
three evolved species together, with matter/geometry fixed. It recomputes
the population-dependent rates, including inelastic energy redistribution,
at each trial. The existing four-moment source solver supplies the inner
radiation update; analytic limits are starting guesses, not accepted roots.
The scattering-free E-v.F equation and the number/momentum equations are
checked independently. Invalid trials are rejected rather than clamped into
a different distribution. The implementation requires ngroups=1, nspecies=3
and the tabulated EOS; it allocates no diagnostic grid functions.

Scheduled opacities and source trials use the same moment-matched FD collision
spectrum and native spectral integrals at the actual comoving moments. There
is no floor-triggered spectrum substitution or secondary LTE Kirchhoff or
mean-energy correction. The scalar collision spectrum does not change the
Minerbo angular transport closure. NuRates transport and radial number fluxes
use the physical number-current projection, including when comoving J is
below the lab-frame energy floor. Numerical state repairs remain separate.
Heavy-flavor coefficients average neutrino/antineutrino absorption/scattering;
emissivity sums two flavors of each. This matters for asymmetric inelastic
kernels. Independent number and energy floors can still imply an unphysical
mean energy; changing the collision spectrum does not validate those initial
conditions or the finite energy quadrature in the atmosphere.

Unrestricted source updates retain the accepted root directly. Limited
semi-implicit updates retain the original baseline, so a zero limiter leaves
it unchanged. The source limiter must remain disabled for NuRates IMEX;
numerical post-source repairs are not included in its implicit increment.
WeakRates/FakeRates retain their original source paths.

The process-separated native coefficients retain pair-process electron-lepton
balance without independent electron-flavor Kirchhoff replacements. Matter
remains fixed during each local collision solve; this is not a simultaneous
matter-radiation nonlinear solve. Host/CUDA cold and warm captured-cell replays
have passed. The current transport-current and test changes have also compiled
with CUDA and completed a four-MPI-rank/four-GPU, two-step poisoned-grid smoke
with finite stored norms. Full-resolution profiling and longer TOV validation
are separate tests; local source and small-grid checks do not establish stellar
stability, accuracy or finite-quadrature convergence. The subsequent
full-resolution TOV profiling attempt aborted in the coupled NuRates source
from a floor-sized radiation state before completing its requested iteration
window. It is a failed validation, not a performance result; the failure
requires investigation before treating this branch as production-ready.
